userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: Kirchhoff's junction and loop rules turn a two-loop circuit into a solvable set of equations: currents must balance at every junction, and signed potential changes must sum to zero around every closed path.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Labeling nodes is not decoration — it converts a picture of wires into a bookkeeping system where each junction gives a current equation and each closed loop gives a signed voltage equation, and together they pin down every unknown current.
DEMO STEPS: 9 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
{
  "concept": "Kirchhoff's junction and loop rules turn a two-loop circuit into a solvable set of equations: currents must balance at every junction, and signed potential changes must sum to zero around every closed path.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Outer rectangle wire frame forming the circuit boundary",
    "Single vertical middle wire dividing the rectangle into a left loop and a right loop",
    "Blue zigzag resistor R1 = 3.00 Ω on the top-left wire segment",
    "Blue zigzag resistor R3 = 3.00 Ω on the top-right wire segment",
    "Blue zigzag resistor R2 = 3.00 Ω on the vertical middle branch",
    "Blue zigzag resistor R4 = 4.00 Ω on the right vertical wire",
    "Plain conducting left vertical wire (no component)",
    "Battery symbol V1 = 24.00 V on the bottom-left wire, + terminal on the left, − on the right",
    "Battery symbol V2 = 29.00 V on the bottom-right wire, − terminal on the left, + on the right",
    "Teal node dots at six points: top-left, top-middle, top-right, bottom-left, bottom-middle, bottom-right",
    "Italic node letters a (top-left), b (top-middle), c (top-right), f (bottom-left), e (bottom-middle), d (bottom-right)",
    "Panel captions (a) unlabeled circuit and (b) lettered circuit",
    "Current arrows I1 (left branch), I2 (middle branch), I3 (right branch) shown on demand",
    "Junction equation callout box (e.g. I1 + I2 = I3)",
    "Loop-rule accumulator panel listing signed terms as the traversal proceeds",
    "Highlight glow used to mark the active branch, resistor, or battery"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "labelView",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "Circuit view",
      "options": [
        "(a) unlabeled",
        "(b) lettered nodes"
      ],
      "default": "(a) unlabeled",
      "teaches": "Node letters and dots are analysis scaffolding drawn onto an unchanged physical circuit, not new components."
    },
    {
      "id": "junctionPick",
      "type": "click",
      "teaches": "At a junction where three branches meet, the currents entering equal the currents leaving, giving one independent equation per junction (b and e give the same equation)."
    },
    {
      "id": "loopTrace",
